ESPHome External Components
Fuzzy Logic Controller & MLX90640 Thermal Camera

This repository provides custom ESPHome external components for building advanced ESP32-based devices such as:

Intelligent fuzzy-logic temperature controllers

Thermal camera systems with real-time heatmap rendering on LVGL displays

The components integrate directly into ESPHome using external_components and are intended for advanced automation, control, and visualization projects.

Components
fuzzy_logic

A wrapper around the eFLL (Embedded Fuzzy Logic Library) that exposes a fuzzy controller object to ESPHome lambdas.

Features

Multiple fuzzy inputs and outputs

Arbitrary fuzzy sets and rules

Runtime fuzzification and defuzzification

Ideal for smooth control (heaters, fans, motors, power control)

The component does not create sensors or outputs by itself.
All interaction is done via lambdas.

mlx90640

External component for the MLX90640 32×24 infrared thermal camera.

Features

Access to raw thermal pixel data

Built-in min / max / mean / median temperature sensors

Designed for thermal image generation

Optimized for LVGL-based displays

Installation

Add the components using ESPHome external_components:

external_components:
  - source:
      type: local
      path: components
    components:
      - fuzzy_logic
      - mlx90640


You may also reference the repository directly from GitHub.

MLX90640 Thermal Camera Example (LVGL Heatmap)

This example shows how to render a live thermal image using LVGL.

Add the Thermal Sensor
mlx90640:
  id: termal
  i2c_id: ext_bus
  update_interval: 500ms
  address: 0x33
  refresh_rate: 0x05   # 0x05 = 16Hz, 0x04 = 8Hz, 0x03 = 4Hz

  min_temperature:
    id: min_temp
  max_temperature:
    id: max_temp
  median_temperature:
    id: mdian_temp
  mean_temperature:
    id: mean_temp

LVGL Image Placeholder
lvgl:
  pages:
    - id: main_page
      widgets:
        - image:
            id: thermal_img
            src: boot_image
            width: 100%
            height: 100%
            align: center
            scrollable: false

Periodic Heatmap Update
interval:
  - interval: 1s
    then:
      - lambda: |-
          generate_heat_map();

Heatmap Generation (Project Include)

Add the following code to a project include file (for example heatmap.h).

Ironbow Color Palette
static const uint16_t ironbow[256] = {
  /* palette data */
};

Heatmap Rendering Function
void generate_heat_map(void)
{
    if (nullptr == heatmap_buf)
        return;

    float *raw_temps = nullptr;
    if (!termal->get_raw_pixels(&raw_temps))
        return;

    const uint16_t *col_map = ironbow;

    float min_t = id(min_temp).state;
    float max_t = id(max_temp).state;
    float inv_range = (max_t != min_t) ? (255.0f / (max_t - min_t)) : 0.0f;

    for (int y = 0; y < out_h; y++) {
        for (int x = 0; x < out_w; x++) {

            float gy = x * (23.0f / (out_w - 1));
            float gx = y * (31.0f / (out_h - 1));

            int x0 = (int)gx;
            int x1 = (x0 < 31) ? x0 + 1 : 31;
            float dx = gx - x0;

            int y0 = (int)gy;
            int y1 = (y0 < 23) ? y0 + 1 : 23;
            float dy = gy - y0;

            float p00 = raw_temps[y0 * 32 + x0];
            float p10 = raw_temps[y0 * 32 + x1];
            float p01 = raw_temps[y1 * 32 + x0];
            float p11 = raw_temps[y1 * 32 + x1];

            float temp = p00 * (1.0f - dx) * (1.0f - dy) +
                         p10 * dx * (1.0f - dy) +
                         p01 * (1.0f - dx) * dy +
                         p11 * dx * dy;

            int color_idx = (int)((temp - min_t) * inv_range);
            if (color_idx < 0) color_idx = 0;
            if (color_idx > 255) color_idx = 255;

            uint16_t c = col_map[color_idx];
            heatmap_buf[y * out_w + x] = (c << 8) | (c >> 8);
        }
    }

    termal->put_raw_pixels();
    lv_obj_invalidate(thermal_img);
}

Fuzzy Logic Controller Example

This example shows a multi-input fuzzy heater controller.

ESP-IDF Configuration (Recommended)
esp32:
  board: wemos_d1_mini32
  framework:
    type: esp-idf

Declare the Fuzzy Controller
fuzzy_logic:
  id: fuzzy_controller

Configure Fuzzy Logic on Boot

All fuzzy sets, inputs, outputs, and rules are defined once at startup:

esphome:
  on_boot:
    - priority: 300
      then:
        - lambda: |-
            auto fuzzy = id(fuzzy_controller).get();
            ESP_LOGV("fuzzy", "boot fuzzy: %#p", fuzzy);

Feed Inputs and Compute Output
sensor:
  - platform: template
    id: fuzzy_sens
    lambda: |-
      auto fuzzy = id(fuzzy_controller).get();

      float rate = id(speed_temperature).state;
      float target = id(current_temperature).state -
                     id(target_temperature).state;

      fuzzy->setInput(1, rate);
      fuzzy->setInput(2, target);

      fuzzy->fuzzify();
      return fuzzy->defuzzify(1);
    update_interval: 1s

Use the Output
output:
  - platform: template
    id: heater_output
    type: float

Summary
Component	Purpose	Result
mlx90640	Thermal imaging	Live heatmap + statistics
fuzzy_logic	Intelligent control logic	Smooth adaptive output
